IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-amendment`

-- ccc22-tests-amendment.l4 -- tests for ccc22-amendment.l4 (sections 601 to 605). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Section 601`

-- (1): args: the objection is for a defect apparent on the face, taken by motion to quash, the accused has entered a plea, leave of the court.
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the objection may be taken` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- by motion to quash before the plea
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the objection may be taken` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the plea but not by motion to quash
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the objection may be taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the plea: "only by leave of the court"
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the objection may be taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after the plea, with leave
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the objection may be taken` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a defect apparent on the face
-- (1), amendment: args: an objection is taken, the court considers it necessary.
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the court may order the indictment or count to be amended to cure the defect` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the court may order the indictment or count to be amended to cure the defect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 601(1) the court may order the indictment or count to be amended to cure the defect` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): args: a trial of an indictment, a variance between the evidence and a count.
#ASSERT `s 601(2) the court may amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(2) the court may amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where there is a variance"
#ASSERT `s 601(2) the court may amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): args: the defect, the matters to be alleged are disclosed by the evidence.
#ASSERT `s 601(3) the court must amend the indictment or count as may be necessary` `s 601(3)(a) the indictment has been preferred under a particular Act of Parliament instead of another Act of Parliament` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): no condition about the evidence
#ASSERT `s 601(3) the court must amend the indictment or count as may be necessary` `s 601(3)(b) the indictment or a count fails to state or states defectively anything requisite to constitute the offence, does not negative an exception that should be negatived, or is in any way defective in substance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(3) the court must amend the indictment or count as may be necessary` `s 601(3)(b) the indictment or a count fails to state or states defectively anything requisite to constitute the offence, does not negative an exception that should be negatived, or is in any way defective in substance` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): "and the matters to be alleged in the proposed amendment are disclosed by the evidence"
#ASSERT `s 601(3) the court must amend the indictment or count as may be necessary` `s 601(3)(c) the indictment or a count is in any way defective in form` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 601(3) the court must amend the indictment or count as may be necessary` `s 601(3) none of those` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where it appears"
-- (4): args: preliminary-inquiry evidence considered, there is evidence taken on the trial, trial evidence considered, circumstances considered, misled or prejudiced considered, merits and injustice considered.
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) "the evidence taken on the trial, if any": there is none
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) there is trial evidence and the court has not considered it
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (e)
-- (4.1): args: the variance is with respect to, proved within the period of limitation, proved within the territorial jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `s 601(4.1) the variance is material` `s 601(4.1)(a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not material"
#ASSERT `s 601(4.1) the variance is material` `s 601(4.1)(a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the period of limitation is not proved: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 601(4.1) the variance is material` `s 601(4.1)(b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 601(4.1) the variance is material` `s 601(4.1)(b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 601(4.1) the variance is material` `s 601(4.1) something else` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): args: in the opinion of the court the accused has been misled or prejudiced, the court's opinion that an adjournment may remove it.
#ASSERT `s 601(5) the court may adjourn the proceedings to a specified day or sittings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(5) the court may adjourn the proceedings to a specified day or sittings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if it is of the opinion that the misleading or prejudice may be removed by an adjournment"
#ASSERT `s 601(5) the court may adjourn the proceedings to a specified day or sittings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where, in the opinion of the court" (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 601(5) the court may make an order with respect to the payment of costs resulting from the necessity for amendment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(5) the court may make an order with respect to the payment of costs resulting from the necessity for amendment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 601(6) the question is a question of law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(6) the question is a question of law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 601(7) the order is endorsed on the indictment as part of the record and the proceedings continue as if the indictment or count had been originally preferred as amended` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(7) the order is endorsed on the indictment as part of the record and the proceedings continue as if the indictment or count had been originally preferred as amended` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8): args: a mistake in the heading, discovered.
#ASSERT `s 601(8) the mistake in the heading must be corrected` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(8) the mistake in the heading must be corrected` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not yet discovered: "as soon as it is discovered"
#ASSERT `s 601(8) the mistake in the heading must be corrected` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 601(8) the mistake in the heading is material` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not material"
#ASSERT `s 601(8) the mistake in the heading is material` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): args: high treason or treason, the offence charged, the amendment adds to the overt acts.
#ASSERT `s 601(9) the authority to amend does not authorize adding to the overt acts` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 100, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- treason
#ASSERT `s 601(9) the authority to amend does not authorize adding to the overt acts` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 50, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(9) the authority to amend does not authorize adding to the overt acts` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 51, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(9) the authority to amend does not authorize adding to the overt acts` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 53, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(9) the authority to amend does not authorize adding to the overt acts` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 52, "") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- sections 50, 51 and 53: not 52
#ASSERT `s 601(9) the authority to amend does not authorize adding to the overt acts` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 100, "") FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no addition to the overt acts
-- (10): args: the body, the proceedings.
#ASSERT `s 601(10) the body is a court for the purposes of section 601` `s 601(10) a court` `s 601(10) summary conviction proceedings` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(10) the body is a court for the purposes of section 601` `s 601(10) a judge` `s 601(10) proceedings on indictment` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(10) the body is a court for the purposes of section 601` `s 601(10) a justice` `s 601(10) proceedings on indictment` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(10) the body is a court for the purposes of section 601` `s 601(10) a provincial court judge` `s 601(10) summary conviction proceedings` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 601(10) the body is a court for the purposes of section 601` `s 601(10) some other body` `s 601(10) proceedings on indictment` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 601(10) the body is a court for the purposes of section 601` `s 601(10) a judge` `s 601(10) other proceedings` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 601(11) section 601 applies to all proceedings, including preliminary inquiries, with such modifications as the circumstances require` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 602 what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 124]"

§ `Section 603`

-- (a): args: ordered to stand trial or at the trial, the thing.
#ASSERT `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` TRUE `s 603(a) the indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` TRUE `s 603(a) the accused’s own statement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` TRUE `s 603(a) the evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` TRUE `s 603(a) the exhibits, if any` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` TRUE `s 603(a) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` FALSE `s 603(a) the indictment` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not yet ordered to stand trial and not at trial
-- (b): args: ordered to stand trial or at the trial, pays a reasonable fee under the tariff, the thing.
#ASSERT `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` TRUE TRUE `s 603(b)(i) the evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` TRUE TRUE `s 603(b)(ii) the accused’s own statement, if any` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` TRUE TRUE `s 603(b)(iii) the indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` TRUE FALSE `s 603(b)(i) the evidence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on payment of a reasonable fee"
#ASSERT `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` FALSE TRUE `s 603(b)(i) the evidence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` TRUE TRUE `s 603(b) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 603 the section bars postponing the trial to enable the accused to secure copies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- arg: the court is satisfied that the failure is not attributable to lack of diligence
#ASSERT `s 603 the section bars postponing the trial to enable the accused to secure copies` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless"
#ASSERT `s 604 what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, 1997, c. 18, s. 69]"

§ `Section 605`

-- (1): args: s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction (a MAYBE), s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction (a MAYBE), summary application on behalf of the accused or the prosecutor, days notice, purpose is a test or examination.
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- three days notice is "after three days notice"
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE 10 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- two days notice
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE 3 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE 3 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE 3 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither kind of court
#ASSERT `s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE 3 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 2 does not decide
#ASSERT `s 605(2) the person is guilty of contempt of court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 605(2) the person is guilty of contempt of court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 605(2) the person may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 605(2) the person may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 605(2) the person may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
